Open questions for counsel:
- Confirm "source-available, all rights reserved" is the right posture given the repo is
  currently private on GitHub and only the compiled binary ships publicly. If the source
  repo is ever made public, this license needs re-review — a spectator being able to read
  the code is a different exposure than a collaborator being able to modify it.
- Confirm whether any vendored/bundled third-party code (e.g. `OrbitAccessApp/.build/`
  checkouts such as GRDB.swift) requires attribution in a NOTICE file; those are build
  artifacts, not committed dependencies, but the equivalent declared dependency (GRDB) may
  still need attribution if statically linked into the shipped binary.
